  "document": "Rwandan Revolution\nThe Rwandan Revolution, also known as the Social Revolution or Wind of Destruction (Kinyarwanda: \"muyaga\" ), was a period of ethnic violence in Rwanda from 1959 to 1961 between the Hutu and the Tutsi, two of the three ethnic groups in Rwanda. The revolution saw the country transition from a Belgian colony with a Tutsi monarchy to an independent Hutu-dominated republic."
